From 397b4f422b234b912c8016aa0179651e5980032d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 18:34:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild admin.php into a full admin suite (implements
 NutriTale Admin.dc.html)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Nine real, DB-backed sections — dashboard, recipes, categories, users,
reports, meal plans, analytics, settings, admin profile — replacing the
old single-purpose quick-add page. Matches the Claude Design mockup's
deep-green/gold visual system.

Schema additions (idempotent via install.php on existing DBs too):
- recipes: category, status, updated_at
- users: last_login_at (set on login)
- new tables: content_reports, curated_meal_plans, admin_settings

Where the mockup had numbers with no real backing (categories, "in
review" status, engagement analytics), this wires them to genuine
queries instead (favorites, ratings, meal_plan_items, pantry usage)
rather than keeping fabricated sample data. Settings toggles persist
for real but aren't yet read anywhere else in the app.

New standalone pages: admin_recipe_edit.php (create/edit, any recipe),
admin_user_view.php (role/premium/unlock controls), admin_export.php
(CSV export for recipes/users).

Verified end-to-end against a local MariaDB: fresh install, migration
of an existing DB missing the new columns, and every POST action
(recipe create, settings toggle, report resolve, meal plan create/
toggle, profile save, user role/premium/unlock) — clean with no PHP
warnings/notices anywhere.

